From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:18:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 053/111] Menu actions give the keyboard back to the editor

After View > Fold, Unfold, Fold all or Unfold all, Show whitespace, Show
line endings, Synchronize vertical scrolling, a line ending conversion or
a JSON tool, the first typed key did not reach the editor. These actions
now focus the active text box, like the actions that end in a tab update.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/folding.rs b/src/folding.rs
index f759328..89089b4 100644
--- a/src/folding.rs
+++ b/src/folding.rs
@@ -583,7 +583,8 @@ impl App {
         });
         // Folding the block around the cursor or selection moves it to the header
         leave_folds(&mut *editor);
-        Task::none()
+        // From the View menu the first key would otherwise not reach the editor
+        self.focus_text_box()
     }
 }
 
diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
index d9f9bba..100a2c0 100644
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -933,6 +933,12 @@ impl App {
         Task::none()
     }
 
+    /// Focus the editor of the active tab, e.g. after a menu action: without it the first key
+    /// typed after the menu closes does not reach the editor.
+    pub fn focus_text_box(&self) -> Task<Message> {
+        widget::text_input::focus(self.text_box_id.clone())
+    }
